; ClientHello = {"v": 1, "t": "ClientHello", "versions": [1, 2],
;   "token": "tok", "minIntervalSeconds": 30, "maxIdleSeconds": 120}
; The keepalive pair the client answers as a responder
; (draft-atwood-mimi-keepalive-00 §4.1): 15 x 30 < 4 x 120.
; Keys in RFC 8949 §4.2.1 order, by length then bytes: t, v, token,
; versions, maxIdleSeconds, minIntervalSeconds.
a6                                  ; map, 6 pairs
61 74                               ; "t"
6b 43 6c 69 65 6e 74 48 65 6c 6c 6f ; "ClientHello" (11)
61 76                               ; "v"
01                                  ; 1
65 74 6f 6b 65 6e                   ; "token"
63 74 6f 6b                         ; "tok"
68 76 65 72 73 69 6f 6e 73          ; "versions"
82                                  ; array, 2 items
01                                  ; 1
02                                  ; 2
6e 6d 61 78 49 64 6c 65 53 65 63 6f 6e 64 73 ; "maxIdleSeconds" (14)
18 78                               ; 120
72                                  ; text, 18 bytes
6d 69 6e 49 6e 74 65 72 76 61 6c    ; "minInterval"
53 65 63 6f 6e 64 73                ; "Seconds"
18 1e                               ; 30
